<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aristobulus of Chalcis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aristobulus of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalcis">Chalcis</a> was a Herodian prince, a great-grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-the-great">Herod the Great</a> and son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-of-chalcis">Herod of Chalcis</a>. In the mid-50s CE the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nero">Nero</a> made him king of Lesser <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a>, and from 57 he also ruled Chalcis in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>. He married Salome, the daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herodias">Herodias</a>, and supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in its eastern wars, including the annexation of Commagene in 72 CE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aristobulus-of-chalcis.jpg" alt="Aristobulus of Chalcis" width="320" height="155" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aristoboulos_king_of_Lesser_Armenia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
